{
  "eval": {
    "slug": "aa-omniscience",
    "displayName": "AA-Omniscience",
    "aliases": ["AA-Omniscience Index"],
    "description": "Artificial Analysis benchmark for factual recall and knowledge calibration across 6,000 questions in 42 topics and six domains. Models answer without tools and are told to abstain when unsure. A grading model labels each reply correct, partially correct, incorrect, or not attempted. The Omniscience Index is 100 × (correct − incorrect) / N on a −100 to 100 scale; cards also report accuracy and hallucination (or non-hallucination) rates. A 600-question public subset is released; the full set is held out.",
    "summary": "Measures whether the model answers factual questions correctly and says it does not know when unsure.",
